#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# to_rules

#% text
# `to_rules(a)` gives the entries of the association `a` as a list of rules `k -> v`, in order.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
to_rules(assoc("x" -> 1, "y" -> 2))
#% output
#= ["x" -> 1, "y" -> 2]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Rules can then be used for replacement:

#% cell
a^2 + b /. to_rules(assoc(a -> 3, b -> 4))
#% output
#= 13

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `assoc`, `keys`, `values`
